WEBVTT


00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.180
This is the main culture difference you encounter

00:00:02.181 --> 00:00:04.061
when travelling in Japan versus South Korea.

00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:06.181
Japan and Korea are two of my favourite countries

00:00:06.182 --> 00:00:07.181
with many similarities,

00:00:07.182 --> 00:00:09.581
but one significant difference that every traveller should know

00:00:09.582 --> 00:00:12.581
is that Korea tends to cater more to larger groups when dining out,

00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:15.601
while Japan is more accommodating to individuals and introverts.

00:00:15.602 --> 00:00:18.601
In Japan, it's completely normal to visit a restaurant just by yourself.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.100
All the sushi, ramen,

00:00:20.101 --> 00:00:23.301
and even barbecue places I visited were all welcoming solo diners.

00:00:23.302 --> 00:00:27.121
In contrast, Korean cuisine and culture often emphasizes shared dishes.

00:00:27.122 --> 00:00:29.621
It can be seen in all the side dishes served in traditional

00:00:29.622 --> 00:00:32.221
restaurants. And many places have minimum orders for two people,

00:00:32.222 --> 00:00:33.621
so if you go there completely alone

00:00:33.622 --> 00:00:36.181
you often have to pay for double the portion and double the price

00:00:36.182 --> 00:00:36.901
on top of that.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.581
Many people will probably feel quite uncomfortable eating alone

00:00:39.582 --> 00:00:41.521
in a restaurant surrounded by groups of people.

00:00:41.522 --> 00:00:42.421
In Japan, however,

00:00:42.422 --> 00:00:44.701
I usually prefer to go out for food just by myself

00:00:44.702 --> 00:00:46.861
because it's easier to get a seat in one of the low key

00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:48.621
small restaurants, especially in the big cities,

00:00:48.622 --> 00:00:51.101
and you get to chat with the chef when you sit at the bar counter.

00:00:51.102 --> 00:00:52.101
Overall, I personally

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:53.661
think Korea is a fantastic country

00:00:53.662 --> 00:00:55.301
for having fun with a large group of friends,

00:00:55.302 --> 00:00:57.661
while Japan is more friendly for singles and solo travellers.

00:00:57.662 --> 00:00:59.621
These are just my personal observations though,

00:00:59.622 --> 00:01:00.861
so if you've been to both countries

00:01:00.862 --> 00:01:02.488
I'd love To hear about your experiences
